R ¶ __At the beginning of Morning Prayer, the Minister shall read with__
  __a loud voice some one, or more of these Sentences of the Scriptures__
  __that follow; And then he shall say that which is written after the__
  __said Sentences.__
I WHEN the wicked man turneth away
  from his wickedness that he hath com-
  mitted, and doeth that which is lawful and right,
  he shall save his soul alive. __Ezek.__ xviii. 27.
P I acknowledge my transgressions, and my sin
  is ever before me. __Psal.__ li. 3.
P Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all
  mine iniquities. __Psal.__ li. 9.
P The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit: a
  broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt
  not despise. __Psal.__ li. 17.
P Rend your heart, and not your garments, and
  turn unto the Lord your God: for he is gracious
  and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kind-
  ness, and repenteth him of the evil. __Joel__ ii. 13.
P To the Lord our God belong mercies and
  forgivenesses, though we have rebelled against
